{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/438564-werewolf-chronicle-in-tokyo-inspired-by-the-warriors","id":438564,"title":"Werewolf Chronicle in Tokyo inspired by The Warriors","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-12T09:39:05-07:00","id":438564,"title":"Werewolf Chronicle in Tokyo inspired by The Warriors","content":"Hi there!<br /> <br /> I'm planning on running a chronicle of Werewolf the Forsaken 2nd ed. for my usual group set in Tokyo.<br /> <br /> The argument is based on the movie The Warriors: Most of the packless Werewolves of Tokyo and all the members of the two great Packs (Few Against Many and 36Love) plus the most recent Pack (my players) would be invited by the leader of Few Against Many to atend to a great reunion in order to trying to organize the scattered Uratha of Tokyo. During this meeting, said leader will be murdered (I'm thinking high-powered sniper rifle with silver bullet should do the trick). The characters will be accused of that murder and hunted down through Tokyo by the rest of the attendants to the meeting, while they try to clean their name and find the actual culprits.<br /> <br /> Problems I'm facing:<br /> <br /> <b>Super detect lies Gift:</b> ok, how to avoid just going out to a Half-Moon and asking if what they say about being innocent is true or not? Are there any loopholes to the power I'm not seeing? Would count as true if they where brainwashed trough Dominate or similar powers to think they commited or planned the murder?<br /> <br /> <b>Who did it, really?:</b> I'm not sure who I actually want to be behind the murder. Some of my options include the third in command in the Few Against Many with help of 36Love, so they can keep being the most organized and influent werewolves around and the traitor from FAM gets to (try to) claim the position of leader.<br /> Other options include:<br /> <br /> 1) The Zaibatsu, maybe even Hototogisu as disorganized werewolves are more easily aproachable and used.<br /> <br /> 2) The voayager cults influenced by the spirits, they like things as they are now, organized werewolves are dangerous.<br /> <br /> 3) The Pure or Bale Hounds, for different reasons.<br /> <br /> Ideas?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T04:39:46-07:00","id":441189,"title":"","content":"Bump, because I still hope someone has any advice and a small update now that my players almost finished with character and pack creation:<br /> <br /> This a small pack, composed of 3 Werewolves, 3 Wolf-Blooded and 9 humans in the periphery.<br /> <br /> The Werewolves are:<br /> <br /> <b>An Iron Master Elodoth:</b> living on the streets of Tokyo as young petty criminal, was later taken from the streets by a nice owner of a profitable family business. He grew up working as his bodyguard, but feeling as if he were his son (all at the same time as being secretely in love with his father figure's actual daughter). A criminal organization pushed to buy the bussiness but the man refused time and time again until he was murdered and his daughter suposedly kidnapped (in front of the character, that failed as a bodyguard) after wich the new administration decided to sell. He is obsesed with finding out where his love is and to seek vengance an attonement for his failure. He has gone from petty job to petty job among criminal circles to better look for the responsibles.<br /> <br /> <b>A Storm Lord/Lady Cahalith:</b> an androginous and asexual son/daughter of the owners of a relatively small videogame company. Has an older sister. He/she works part time in Host club for the kicks of it, as he/she likes to be the center of atention and longing even if he/she is incapable of feeling such. I'm planning on some sub-company of the Hototogisu trying to buy his/her parents company in an attempt to blackmail him/her into revvealing werewolf secrets. As you probably imagine the ambigous gender is a great part of the characters identity.<br /> <br /> <b>A Huntress in Darkness Ithaeur:</b> A miko in charge of a small and (I picture it as such) rather ruinous temple. She tries her best to keep the place in a good shape and keep the donatives and prayers flowing. The temple has a terrible case of Azlu infestation and that's why the spirits are particularly few and weak there. She still doesn't know that, the first sign that something is wrong willbe after her First Change when she can actually take a look at the Shadow there.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}